1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
This video guide will get you up and running with Burp Suite Enterprise Edition as quickly as possible.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:16,000
We'll show you how to download and install the software and get to the point where you're ready to perform your first scan of a site.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Specifically, this guide explains how to perform a standard single machine deployment of Burp Suite Enterprise Edition using the default settings.

4
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:31,000
This configuration is most useful for trials or if you just want to see what Burp Suite Enterprise Edition can do.

5
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:39,000
For the best experience, we recommend starting out on a machine with at least 8 CPU cores and 24GB of RAM.

6
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:46,000
You can find the latest version of Burp Suite Enterprise Edition on the releases page of our website or your account page.

7
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:53,000
Launch the Burp Suite Enterprise Edition installer in the normal way for your operating system.

8
00:00:53,000 --> 00:01:00,000
In the installation wizard, keep clicking next to accept the default options until you are prompted to choose a port for the web server.

9
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:07,000
By default, port 8080 is used but you may need to select a different one if this isn't available on your machine.

10
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Keep clicking next to accept the default for all remaining options until the installation process begins.

11
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Please note that this may take a few minutes.

12
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:20,000
If prompted, allow Java to accept incoming connections.

13
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:26,000
Once you have installed Burp Suite Enterprise Edition, you will need to perform some additional configuration in the app itself.

14
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:33,000
To access the configuration page, visit HTTP localhost port 8080 in your browser.

15
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:39,000
When you first access Burp Suite Enterprise Edition, you're prompted to create an initial admin user.

16
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Enter your email address and a secure password.

17
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:47,000
We recommend leaving the default username as administrator.

18
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Do keep a note of these credentials.

19
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:54,000
You need them to complete the initial setup and they're not easily recovered if you lose them.

20
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Click finish and login to complete the configuration process and open the sign-in page.

21
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Log in using the administrator user that you created in the installation wizard.

22
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:06,000
If you've forgotten these credentials, you need to reset your password via the command line.

23
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:12,000
The first time you launch Burp Suite Enterprise Edition, you need to activate your license.

24
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:18,000
If you don't have one yet, you can sign up for a free trial or purchase a full license from our website.

25
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:23,000
To activate your license, Burp Suite Enterprise Edition needs to connect to portswigger.net.

26
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:30,000
If you can only access the public web via a proxy server, click Configure Proxy Settings to enable this connection first.

27
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:42,000
When prompted, upload your license to get instructed.

28
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:48,000
Once your license is activated, click Continue to begin the onboarding wizard.

29
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:52,000
This will guide you through the process of running your first scan.

